00:03:30.009 --> 00:03:31.610
I think another thing we can do though

62
00:03:31.610 --> 00:03:36.610
in order to control how contrasty this noise is,

63
00:03:38.469 --> 00:03:44.659
is add in a step node and I'll set this to 0.5 as well.

64
00:03:46.319 --> 00:03:52.199
This is gonna make it a little more of a hard transition

65
00:03:52.199 --> 00:03:55.580
when we're going from black to white.

66
00:03:55.580 --> 00:03:56.419
This looks good.

67
00:03:56.419 --> 00:04:00.379
We can set this to the side a little bit more over here.

68
00:04:00.379 --> 00:04:03.719
Now what I'd like to do is set this color.

69
00:04:03.719 --> 00:04:07.639
We're gonna pick this to be, double click here,

70
00:04:07.639 --> 00:04:11.939
say let's go, we used pink and green

71
00:04:11.939 --> 00:04:14.460
or purple and green, let's go purple.

72
00:04:14.460 --> 00:04:16.839
And then another color here,

73
00:04:16.839 --> 00:04:20.459
we can just duplicate that with control D,

74
00:04:20.459 --> 00:04:24.860
click and we can pick our color from four, awesome.

75
00:04:24.860 --> 00:04:26.899
So in order to switch between these two colors,

