84
00:04:51.329 --> 00:04:53.970
it will show whatever this,

85
00:04:53.970 --> 00:04:56.449
the output of just this specific node.

86
00:04:57.759 --> 00:05:02.060
So this is like a blend now between our light purple

87
00:05:02.060 --> 00:05:04.060
and our light green.

88
00:05:04.060 --> 00:05:08.699
So if we wanna combine this with our texture down here,

89
00:05:08.699 --> 00:05:13.779
we can use a multiply,

90
00:05:13.779 --> 00:05:15.560
auto multiply, so make sure you just get

91
00:05:15.560 --> 00:05:17.519
the basic one for this.

92
00:05:18.339 --> 00:05:20.500
We'll plug this in, plug that into base color,

93
00:05:20.500 --> 00:05:25.540
stop previewing, and now we've got our color

94
00:05:25.540 --> 00:05:26.899
applied to our noise.

95
00:05:26.899 --> 00:05:29.009
If we put this down to zero,

96
00:05:29.009 --> 00:05:31.930
you can see we're all the way at purple

97
00:05:31.930 --> 00:05:33.810
and if we put this to one,

98
00:05:33.810 --> 00:05:38.180
we're all the way to green, awesome.

99
00:05:38.180 --> 00:05:43.329
We can apply this, and then in order to be able

100
00:05:43.329 --> 00:05:48.360
to change this color, what we need to do

101
00:05:48.360 --> 00:05:53.980
is make this a constant.

102
00:05:53.980 --> 00:05:55.779
So this will allow us to set,

103
00:05:55.779 --> 00:05:58.000
if we, and then a parameter,

104
00:05:58.000 --> 00:06:06.579
and we will call this color one, two, two.

105
00:06:10.699 --> 00:06:15.519
So now, change the value of this parameter,

106
00:06:15.519 --> 00:06:20.879
it will change the value of our material.

107
00:06:22.870 --> 00:06:25.069
And then one last thing for now,

108
00:06:25.089 --> 00:06:36.509
we are going to come down here to another multiply

109
00:06:36.509 --> 00:06:40.269
and we will pipe in another parameter here,

110
00:06:41.230 --> 00:06:44.439
constant, convert to parameter,

111
00:06:44.439 --> 00:06:49.439
and we will call this glow intensity,

112
00:06:52.579 --> 00:06:55.959
set this to something like five,

113
00:06:55.959 --> 00:07:00.170
and then hook this up to our emissive color.

114
00:07:00.170 --> 00:07:02.389
And so now this is going to allow our material

115
00:07:02.430 --> 00:07:07.430
to have an effect on the Lumen global illumination system.

116
00:07:09.189 --> 00:07:12.089
And from here, we'll get to see our cubes

117
00:07:12.089 --> 00:07:16.920
and our stage pillars generating patterns

118
00:07:16.920 --> 00:07:22.149
as our glowing cubes are able to go from zero to one.

119
00:07:22.149 --> 00:07:25.569
So this is all well and good

120
00:07:25.569 --> 00:07:30.000
and we can actually convert these to parameters

121
00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:34.199
so that they can change in material instances.

122
00:07:34.199 --> 00:07:35.959
And you do that just by right-clicking

123
00:07:36.000 --> 00:07:39.470
and telling them to convert to parameters.

124
00:07:39.470 --> 00:07:40.949
In order to make this interactive,

125
00:07:40.949 --> 00:07:45.949
we're gonna need a way to change the color of our,

126
00:07:47.029 --> 00:07:48.629
or change that number that controls

127
00:07:48.629 --> 00:07:50.750
the color of our cubes dynamically.

128
00:07:51.610 --> 00:07:54.149
There are a couple ways of changing the value

129
00:07:54.149 --> 00:07:57.209
of a parameter on a material at runtime.

130
00:07:57.209 --> 00:08:01.850
One of them is by using a dynamic instance of the material

131
00:08:01.850 --> 00:08:04.509
or the other way is by using

132
00:08:04.529 --> 00:08:06.529
a material parameter collection.

133
00:08:07.370 --> 00:08:09.850
We're gonna look at this material parameter collection

134
00:08:09.850 --> 00:08:12.329
cause it's one of the unique assets

135
00:08:12.329 --> 00:08:14.810
and part of the Unreal Engine workflow

136
00:08:14.810 --> 00:08:16.490
that can be really powerful.

137
00:08:17.670 --> 00:08:20.149
It's designed for being able to update

138
00:08:20.149 --> 00:08:23.610
large groups of materials simultaneously,

139
00:08:23.610 --> 00:08:25.970
but we're just gonna see how it works with the one here

140
00:08:25.970 --> 00:08:28.470
cause it gives us a little bit more flexibility

141
00:08:28.470 --> 00:08:29.310
in our code.

142
00:08:30.480 --> 00:08:33.440
So we're gonna be creating it in the content browser,

143
00:08:33.440 --> 00:08:34.620
creating a new parameter,

144
00:08:34.620 --> 00:08:36.860
and then we can add it to our material

145
00:08:36.860 --> 00:08:39.720
that we were just working on.

146
00:08:39.720 --> 00:08:41.980
Over here, I'll right-click,

147
00:08:41.980 --> 00:08:45.470
I'll go to material and we see

148
00:08:45.470 --> 00:08:49.379
in material parameter collection,

149
00:08:49.379 --> 00:08:56.580
I'll call this MPC session blur change, fantastic.

150
00:09:01.720 --> 00:09:04.220
We'll open this up and we can see all we're doing

151
00:09:04.220 --> 00:09:06.179
is putting in a list of scalar parameters.

152
00:09:06.179 --> 00:09:11.179
So just one float value or a vector parameter,

153
00:09:11.240 --> 00:09:15.279
so an array of float values.

154
00:09:15.279 --> 00:09:16.840
In this case, we create one

155
00:09:16.840 --> 00:09:27.080
and I'll call this color change,

156
00:09:27.080 --> 00:09:32.730
we can call this info

157
00:09:32.730 --> 00:09:36.679
and this is the default value of zero, which is fine.

158
00:09:36.679 --> 00:09:39.700
Now back over here in our color map

159
00:09:39.700 --> 00:09:41.360
or in our material,

160
00:09:41.360 --> 00:09:47.230
we can look for a parameter collection parameter.

161
00:09:53.059 --> 00:09:54.539
It's already seen that we want

162
00:09:54.539 --> 00:09:56.919
to get our session color change

163
00:09:56.919 --> 00:09:59.860
and we will grab our value for A to B

164
00:09:59.860 --> 00:10:06.620
and then instead of using the parameter in the material,

165
00:10:06.740 --> 00:10:09.899
we will use this material parameter collection.

166
00:10:12.970 --> 00:10:14.570
Perfect, so this is gonna allow us

167
00:10:14.570 --> 00:10:17.789
to change the value, have our other blueprints

168
00:10:17.789 --> 00:10:20.990
change the value here in this asset

169
00:10:20.990 --> 00:10:23.889
and that will be propagated to any material

170
00:10:23.889 --> 00:10:26.789
that incorporates that same parameter.

171
00:10:30.409 --> 00:10:32.409
For this, we're gonna do it in the level blueprint

172
00:10:32.409 --> 00:10:35.049
and then we're gonna migrate it

173
00:10:35.049 --> 00:10:40.759
into a new third person character.

174
00:10:40.879 --> 00:10:42.799
In the next video, we'll look at how the player

175
00:10:42.799 --> 00:10:46.320
